      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To investigate the association of restricted usage of repertoire of T cell receptor V beta (TCR V beta) with asthma."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "In 36 Chinese asthmatics, peripheral blood TCR V beta was studied by means of fluorescein-labeled RT-PCR as well as genescan and genotype software analysis. The clonality of the predominant usage T cell receptors was analyzed by denaturing gel electrophoresis and single strand conformation polymorphism (SSCP) by using genescan analysis (with 377 ABI DNA sequencer)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The number of cases predominantly using TCRV beta 8 gene families in asthmatics and those allergy to house dust mite (HDM) was significantly higher than that of normal controls (P = 0.0230, 0.0147), and so the TCR V beta 5.1 gene family for asthmatics allergic to HDM (P = 0.0186). It is remarkable-that only two cases in 36 asthmatics were allergic to ragweed and both of them predominantly used TCR V beta 1 gene families. The TCR V beta gene families predominantly used in asthmatics showed polyclonal expression in all normal controls and most asthmatics, but 5 asthmatics showed oligoclonal expression of TCR V beta 8 gene families."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "TCRV beta 8 and TCR V beta 5.1 gene families may be associated with allergy to HDM in asthmatics. TCR V beta gene families in asthmatic peripheral blood showed oligoclonal expression tendency."
        }
      ]},
